WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.517 --> 00:00:02.700
- [Narrator] "Banks are not your friends."

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.650
That's Alex Mashinsky in the shirt,

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.810
founder and CEO of Celsius,

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.840
one of the largest
crypto lending platforms.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:10.980
And on June 12th,

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.020
his company surprised customers

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.730
when it unexpectedly announced

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:17.640
it was pausing all withdrawals,
swaps, and transfers

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.690
between accounts

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.970
due to extreme market conditions.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:21.803
For reference,

00:00:21.803 --> 00:00:24.630
this year, Bitcoin has lost
more than half of its value

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.820
and another popular cryptocurrency Ether

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.160
has fallen around 70%.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:33.090
- Celsius decision to
freeze customer accounts

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.360
has rippled across the
cryptocurrency industry.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.790
Shortly after its announcement,

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:43.140
another Asia-based crypto
lender called Babel Finance

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:46.500
announced that it is also
suspending withdrawals.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.990
- [Narrator] Unlike banks,
which are FDIC insured,

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:50.730
crypto lenders like Celsius

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.110
lack the legal protections

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.960
that are built into the
traditional financial system.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.540
And as the crypto market
continues to tumble,

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.510
many users of Celsius
and the exchange Coinbase

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.287
are beginning to wonder,

00:01:02.287 --> 00:01:04.590
"If these crypto platforms go bankrupt,

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:06.567
what happens to my assets?"

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.680
Celsius is one of dozens
of unregulated lenders

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:11.850
and lending platforms

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.530
that have emerged in recent years,

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:15.060
cutting high returns to investors

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.430
who are willing to lend
their digital assets.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:21.720
- Celsius promised customers
annual percentage yields

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.960
as high as 18.6%.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.560
That's a lot more than customers can get

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.900
from regular bank accounts today.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.700
- [Narrator] Here's how that works.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.030
Customers deposit their
cryptocurrency in the Celsius system

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.500
in exchange for a yield.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.020
This is essentially an unsecured loan.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.730
And in order to earn a return,

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:44.370
the company lends out
assets to other users

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.070
and puts customer deposits
in often high yield,

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:50.190
high risk decentralized
finance investments.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:51.930
When the system is working correctly,

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:54.360
Celsius says that customers
can expect approval

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.790
for their withdrawals within 24 hours.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.490
But as cryptocurrency
prices continued to fall,

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:00.960
customers started to withdraw

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.120
at a rate Celsius couldn't keep up with.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:06.900
- Celsius does not have enough liquidity,

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:10.920
meaning readily spendable
cryptocurrency on hand

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.350
to hand back to the customers.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:14.280
- [Narrator] The company has since

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.870
hired restructuring lawyers

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.610
to advise on possible solutions

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.890
for its mounting financial problems.

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:22.350
- One of the financing options

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:24.870
included a financial restructuring,

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.990
meaning that the company
could potentially file

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:29.280
for bankruptcy.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.630
- [Narrator] And if that happens,

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.940
users could face big losses.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.610
According to Celsius's terms of use,

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.400
users that deposit assets
in the earn service

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.350
grant the company "all right and title

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.450
to such eligible digital assets,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.460
including ownership rights."

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.790
That document also calls
out bankruptcy explicitly,

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.490
saying, "In the event that
Celsius becomes bankrupt,

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:51.660
enters liquidation,

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:54.690
or is otherwise unable
to repay its obligations,

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.660
any eligible digital assets
used in the earn service

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.790
or as collateral under the borrow service

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.470
may not be recoverable."

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.180
You will likely not see a line like this

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.620
in a user agreement for a bank,

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.050
since most banks are FDIC insured.

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:10.020
So what does that mean for users?

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.510
- Based on Celsius' terms of use,

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:15.300
in the event of a bankruptcy,

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.330
customer who deposited cryptocurrencies

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.010
into Celsius accounts

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.110
may not be able to get their money back

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.480
because they would be considered

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.790
essentially unsecured creditors

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:31.790
and even if they were to file
for lawsuits against Celsius,

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.550
they might not have a great chance

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:37.440
of winning that legal action.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.420
- [Narrator] Similarly,
the exchange Coinbase

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.910
addressed bankruptcy in
its quarterly filings,

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.880
adding a disclosure based
on SEC accounting guidelines

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.200
released in March.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.420
- Coinbase made the disclosure

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.670
that in the event of a bankruptcy,

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:55.670
the digital assets that
Coinbase holds for its customers

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.620
may not really belong to the customers.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:00.210
- [Narrator] Coinbase
noted that the new language

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.560
in its financial report

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.330
could lead customers to view its service

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.580
as "more risky and less attractive."

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:08.490
- Coinbase CEO Brian
Armstrong has come out

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:11.520
and said that the likelihood
of the company going bankrupt

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.140
is extremely low

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:16.560
and the company is in very
good financial conditions,

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.510
but he made the disclosure

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:21.150
just for the purpose of transparency.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:21.983
- [Narrator] Nearly one month

00:04:21.983 --> 00:04:23.610
after the bankruptcy disclosure,

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.430
on June 14th, Coinbase
announced it was laying off

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.560
around 18% of its workforce.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.300
Armstrong said the decision was made

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.810
to ensure Coinbase's health
during this economic downturn.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.420
But if a crypto platform
like Celsius or Coinbase

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.710
were to go bankrupt,

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.530
it wouldn't be the first
to go under in that way.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.660
In 2014, Mt. Gox,

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:45.570
then the largest crypto
asset platform worldwide,

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:46.710
filed for bankruptcy

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:49.800
before ultimately filing for
liquidation later that year.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:54.690
- The collapse of crypto
exchange Mt. Gox back in 2014

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.850
also rippled across the industry.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:05:00.660
It caused the price of Bitcoin to plummet

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.510
and brought about, so to speak,

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.360
one of the first crypto
winters in the industry.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:07.590
- [Narrator] A rehabilitation plan

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:09.300
for affected Mt. Gox's users

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.880
was not confirmed until last fall.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.620
Cryptocurrency as an industry

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.380
still lacks comparable
regulation and protection

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.840
to traditional financial institutions,

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:21.030
but a recent bill looks to change that.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:24.780
- Senators Cynthia Lummis
and Kirsten Gillibrand

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:27.420
proposed a bipartisan crypto bill

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:30.750
that the Responsible
Financial Innovation Act,

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:35.100
which aims to provide a
comprehensive regulatory framework

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.810
for the crypto industry.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:37.920
- [Narrator] While the bill was released

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:38.940
around the same time

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.190
that Coinbase made its
bankruptcy disclosure,

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:44.190
it is not in direct response
to the platform's announcement.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.810
The bill is not expected to pass

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:48.570
and other lawmakers have
not signed on to it.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:49.620
As for Celsius,

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.750
the company is under investigation.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.490
The Texas State Securities Board

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:56.100
said it has opened an
investigation into Celsius

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.650
over its decision to
freeze customer accounts

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.030
and is working in conjunction

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:03.679
with New Jersey, Kentucky,
Alabama, and Washington.

00:06:03.679 --> 00:06:06.262
(gentle music)

